\title{Single-Source Shortest Paths}
\date{2026-10-03T19:26:22Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Dijkstra's Algorithm solves the \em{single-source shortest path} (SSSP) problem in a [directed](00N6), [weighted](00NP) graph: given a vertex #{s}, find the shortest paths from #{s} to \em{every other} vertex in the graph.}

\p{Note that this seems like a harder problem than just finding the shortest path from #{s} to some particular target vertex #{t}, but it's really not.  Intuitively, you can’t find the shortest path from #{s} to #{t} without exploring the rest of the graph, thus discovering shortest paths from #{s} to other vertices along the way.}


